1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,714
International students often pay tuition
with money from two places:

2
00:00:04,764 --> 00:00:08,608
their own savings abroad and a top-up from
family at home.

3
00:00:08,658 --> 00:00:13,910
Corridor is an AI money agent that turns
one tuition invoice into one verified,

4
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:18,877
approved and tracked payment, and it never
moves money without the owner's

5
00:00:18,927 --> 00:00:19,750
confirmation.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,077
Putri studies in Singapore.

7
00:00:23,127 --> 00:00:31,860
She takes her invoice from the university
portal and gives consent for one check.

8
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:39,775
Corridor verifies the university's digital
signature over the exact file:

9
00:00:39,825 --> 00:00:40,425
VALID.

10
00:00:40,475 --> 00:00:48,340
An edited amount, another student's
invoice or an unknown issuer would be

11
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:49,750
stopped here.

12
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:57,329
Putri has 3,120 Singapore dollars and
keeps 1,500 for rent and food.

13
00:00:57,379 --> 00:01:05,037
So she can contribute 1,620, and her
father Budi needs to add exactly 379

14
00:01:05,087 --> 00:01:06,198
dollars 60.

15
00:01:06,248 --> 00:01:14,750
Paying everything herself is rejected,
because it would break her living reserve.

16
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:19,913
Corridor compares four routes from rupiah.

17
00:01:19,963 --> 00:01:25,584
Route A is cheaper but arrives after the
deadline.

18
00:01:25,634 --> 00:01:31,821
Route C is the cheapest but arrives five
dollars short.

19
00:01:31,871 --> 00:01:34,316
Route D hides its fee.

20
00:01:34,366 --> 00:01:42,935
Route B costs 4,725,000 rupiah, fits
Budi's limit and posts on time with the

21
00:01:42,985 --> 00:01:44,750
required buffer.

22
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:50,827
Each person approves only their own money.

23
00:01:50,877 --> 00:02:00,828
Budi signs in with his own PIN and
approves only the rupiah debit from his

24
00:02:00,878 --> 00:02:01,909
account.

25
00:02:01,959 --> 00:02:08,397
Putri approves the tuition payment with
Face ID.

26
00:02:08,447 --> 00:02:14,344
Both approvals are bound to the plan's
hash:

27
00:02:14,394 --> 00:02:19,750
if anything changes, they are cancelled.

28
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:27,851
Execution uses idempotency keys, so a
retry can never pay twice.

29
00:02:27,901 --> 00:02:33,386
The top-up settles, then the tuition
transfer.

30
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:35,913
But sent is not paid:

31
00:02:35,963 --> 00:02:44,937
the case completes only when the
university posts the payment with a signed

32
00:02:44,987 --> 00:02:45,659
event.

33
00:02:45,709 --> 00:02:49,750
Putri keeps exactly 1,500 dollars.

34
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:54,531
Putri can also ask in her own language.

35
00:02:54,581 --> 00:03:03,068
In Bahasa Indonesia, the agent explains
where her payment is, using the same

36
00:03:03,118 --> 00:03:04,640
verified case.

37
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:13,964
It can read, explain and draft, but it has
no tool to approve, add payees or change

38
00:03:14,014 --> 00:03:14,750
limits.

39
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,959
Here is a scam:

40
00:03:17,009 --> 00:03:26,606
a fake landlord asks her to pay a new
account, with a hidden instruction for the

41
00:03:26,656 --> 00:03:27,812
assistant.

42
00:03:27,862 --> 00:03:36,856
The policy layer marks the turn as
untrusted and refuses any payment draft,

43
00:03:36,906 --> 00:03:39,750
whatever the model says.

44
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:44,424
The operator console simulates real
failures:

45
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:50,408
a revoked invoice, a lost provider
response, a failed transfer.

46
00:03:50,458 --> 00:03:56,297
The case blocks, reconciles or re-plans,
and never pays twice.

47
00:03:56,347 --> 00:04:03,800
If the AI model goes down, a labelled
simplified mode keeps answering read-only

48
00:04:03,850 --> 00:04:04,750
questions.

49
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:15,474
Every action goes into a hash-chained
audit log anchored to a ledger.

50
00:04:15,524 --> 00:04:24,750
If anyone edits a single entry, the Shield
tab shows TAMPERED.

51
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:29,941
We test all of this with one command:

52
00:04:29,991 --> 00:04:39,910
95 automated tests across agent tasks,
attacks, policy bypass, tuition cases,

53
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:44,183
model outage and audit integrity.

54
00:04:44,233 --> 00:04:45,348
Corridor:

55
00:04:45,398 --> 00:04:49,750
money that moves with you, safely.

